From ca0dd84bda639f5aa54e0d0e650d25021cf3c361 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miro Kropacek <miro.kropacek@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 22:54:48 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] BACKENDS: ATARI: Use the new thread scheduler

Fix a couple of potential bugs and make it FreeMiNT friendly, too:

- Preempt only when the interrupted user-mode USP lies within our
  process, otherwise the tick may hijack a foreign process' context;
  possible since MiNT's memory protection doesn't remap addresses.

- If the USP check fails, the interrupted PC is checked as well: the
  code may misuse a7 as a data register (on the other hand, the PC check
  doesn't work well for plugins so both checks are essential).

- The fake tail frame now preserves the interrupted IPL instead of a
  constant 0x2700 which blinded mint_vbl's stacked-SR checks.

- Known limitation: MiNT cannot forcibly timeslice ScummVM while threads
  are on (the tail frame must be a supervisor one); other processes run
  when ScummVM blocks in the kernel.
---
